OL,3,CProgramme listings for TUE 19 MAY
OL,4,G0930FEssential Classics
OL,5,     GGeorgia Mann plays the best in
OL,6,     Gclassical music, with discoveries
OL,7,     Gand surprises rubbing shoulders
OL,8,     Gwith familiar favourites.
OL,9,G1300FClassical Live
OL,10,     GElizabeth Alker introduces an
OL,11,     Gafternoon of specially made
OL,12,     Grecordings including orchestral
OL,13,     Gworks from the Berlin
OL,14,     GPhilharmonic and chamber music
OL,15,     Gled by Sir Antonio Pappano.
OL,16,G1600FComposer of the Week: Palestrina
OL,17,     GAs young Palestrina makes a name
OL,18,     Gfor himself in Rome, Donald
OL,19,     GMacleod opens the venerable score
OL,20,     Gof the Mass which is considered
OL,21,     Gto have marked a turning point in
OL,22,     Gmusic history.
